  "tracks": {
    "single": {
      "label": "Readings",
      "readings": [
        {
          "role": "first",
          "ref": "Isaiah 6:1-8, (9-13)",
          "refKey": "Isa.6.1-Isa.6.8",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "call-and-discipleship",
              "mission-and-witness",
              "prayer-and-worship",
              "repentance"
            ],
            "image": [
              "fire",
              "king-and-throne",
              "trumpet-and-voice"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "fear-and-trembling",
              "wonder-and-awe"
            ],
            "function": [
              "confession",
              "gathering"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 6,
              "v_start": 1,
              "v_end": 1,
              "text": "I saw — In a vision. The Lord - The Divine Majesty as he subsisteth in three persons. His train - His royal and judicial robe; for he is represented as a judge."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 6,
              "v_start": 2,
              "v_end": 2,
              "text": "Stood — As ministers attending upon their Lord. Seraphim - An order of holy angels, thus called from fire and burning, which this word properly signifies; to represent either their nature, which is bright and glorious, subtile, and pure; or their property, of fervent zeal for God's service and glory. Covered - Out of profound reverence."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 6,
              "v_start": 3,
              "v_end": 3,
              "text": "Cried — Singing in consort. Holy - This is repeated thrice, to intimate the Trinity of persons united in the Divine essence. Glory - Of the effects and demonstrations of his glorious holiness, as well as of his power, wisdom, and goodness."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 6,
              "v_start": 4,
              "v_end": 4,
              "text": "The posts — Together with the door itself. Such violent motions were commonly tokens of God's anger. Smoak - Which elsewhere is a token of God's presence and acceptance, but here of his anger."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 6,
              "v_start": 5,
              "v_end": 5,
              "text": "l am — I am a great sinner, as many other ways, so particularly by my lips. I am an unclean branch of an unclean tree; besides my own uncleanness, I have both by my omissions and commissions involved myself in the guilt of their sins. Have seen - The sight of this glorious and holy God gives me cause to fear that he is come to judgment against me."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 6,
              "v_start": 6,
              "v_end": 6,
              "text": "Flew — By God's command. A coal - Both a token and an instrument of purification. The altar - Of burnt-offering."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 6,
              "v_start": 7,
              "v_end": 7,
              "text": "Laid it — So as only to touch my lips, and not to burn them; which God could easily effect. Lo - This is a sign that I have pardoned and purged the uncleanness of thy lips."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 6,
              "v_start": 8,
              "v_end": 8,
              "text": "Who — To deliver the following message. The change of the number, I and us, is very remarkable; and both being meant of one and the same Lord, do sufficiently intimate a plurality of persons in the Godhead."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "psalm",
          "ref": "Psalm 138",
          "refKey": "Ps.138",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "faithfulness",
              "prayer-and-worship",
              "providence-and-care",
              "thanksgiving"
            ],
            "image": [
              "hand-and-arm"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "praise-and-exultation",
              "trust"
            ],
            "function": [
              "praise-opening",
              "thanksgiving-offering"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 138,
              "v_start": 1,
              "v_end": 1,
              "text": "The gods — Before kings and princes."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 138,
              "v_start": 2,
              "v_end": 2,
              "text": "Temple — Where the ark was. He was not permitted to enter into it. Magnified - For thou hast glorified thy word or promise unto me more than any other of thy glorious perfections."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 138,
              "v_start": 4,
              "v_end": 4,
              "text": "The kings — A prophecy of the calling of the Gentiles. Hear - The gospel preached among then."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 138,
              "v_start": 5,
              "v_end": 5,
              "text": "The ways — His wonderful counsel and gracious providences."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 138,
              "v_start": 8,
              "v_end": 8,
              "text": "Perfect — Will finish the great work of my deliverance. Forsake not - Or, do not give over, the work of my salvation, which is thus far advanced, not by any human help, but by thy power and providence. This psalm is, by many of the Jewish doctors, esteemed the most excellent in the whole book. The omniscience of God is here asserted, ver. 1-6. Proved by two arguments; That he is everywhere present, ver. 7-12. And that he made us, ver. 13-16. This may fill us with pleasing admiration of God, ver. 17, 18. With an holy hatred of sin, ver. 19-22. And with an holy satisfaction in our own integrity, ver. 23, 24. To the chief musician, A psalm of David."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "second",
          "ref": "1 Corinthians 15:1-11",
          "refKey": "1Cor.15.1-1Cor.15.11",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "grace",
              "mission-and-witness",
              "resurrection-and-life",
              "word-of-god"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "assurance",
              "praise-and-exultation"
            ],
            "function": [
              "creed-affirmation"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 15,
              "v_start": 2,
              "v_end": 2,
              "text": "Ye are saved, if ye hold fast — Your salvation is begun, and will be perfected, if ye continue in the faith. Unless ye have believed in vain - Unless indeed your faith was only a delusion."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 15,
              "v_start": 3,
              "v_end": 3,
              "text": "I received — From Christ himself. It was not a fiction of my own. Isaiah liii, 8, 9."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 15,
              "v_start": 4,
              "v_end": 4,
              "text": "According to the scriptures — He proves it first from scripture, then from the testimony of a cloud of witnesses. Psalm xvi, 10."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 15,
              "v_start": 5,
              "v_end": 5,
              "text": "By the twelve — This was their standing appellation; but their full number was not then present."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 15,
              "v_start": 6,
              "v_end": 6,
              "text": "Above five hundred — Probably in Galilee. A glorious and incontestable proof! The greater part remain - Alive."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 15,
              "v_start": 7,
              "v_end": 7,
              "text": "Then by all the apostles — The twelve were mentioned ver. 5. This title here, therefore, seems to include the seventy; if not all those, likewise, whom God afterwards sent to plant the gospel in heathen nations."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 15,
              "v_start": 8,
              "v_end": 8,
              "text": "An untimely birth — It was impossible to abase himself more than he does by this single appellation. As an abortion is not worthy the name of a man, so he affirms himself to be not worthy the name of an apostle."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 15,
              "v_start": 9,
              "v_end": 9,
              "text": "I persecuted the church — True believers are humbled all their lives, even for the sins they committed before they believed."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 15,
              "v_start": 10,
              "v_end": 10,
              "text": "I laboured more than they all — That is, more than any of them, from a deep sense of the peculiar love God had shown me. Yet, to speak more properly, it is not I, but the grace of God that is with me - This it is which at first qualified me for the work, and still excites me to zeal and diligence in it."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 15,
              "v_start": 11,
              "v_end": 11,
              "text": "Whether I or they, so we preach — All of us speak the same thing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "gospel",
          "ref": "Luke 5:1-11",
          "refKey": "Luke.5.1-Luke.5.11",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "call-and-discipleship",
              "grace",
              "mission-and-witness"
            ],
            "image": [
              "harvest",
              "sea-and-storm"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "resolve-and-sending",
              "wonder-and-awe"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 5,
              "v_start": 1,
              "v_end": 1,
              "text": "Matt. iv, 18; Mark i, 16."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 5,
              "v_start": 6,
              "v_end": 6,
              "text": "Their net brake — Began to tear."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 5,
              "v_start": 8,
              "v_end": 8,
              "text": "Depart from me, for I am a sinful man — And therefore not worthy to be in thy presence."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 5,
              "v_start": 11,
              "v_end": 11,
              "text": "They forsook all and followed him — They had followed him before, John i, 43, but not so as to forsake all. Till now, they wrought at their ordinary calling."
            }
          ]
        }
